# node-policy-activation.ps1 - the COORDINATED switch-on of the EXISTING platform host policy gate on nucbox-k11-4 (minipc),
# with the wallet hold ALREADY enforced (PowerShell 5.1). Prepared by Claude (platform-activation 20261022) for ROOT; never run by
# its author. Composed by compose.py from the root-accepted rpc-integrated coordinator df2e58f2 (base/node-hold-cutover.ps1):
# every "#@BASE a-b" line range below is copied byte for byte (compose verifies the base sha; tools/test_activation.py proves the
# reused functions identical). Executed ONLY from hash-verified bytes by a one-shot SYSTEM task (root-policy-activation.py), so
# an SSH disconnect cannot interrupt it. Bounded (-BoundSec). Every step appends ONE JSON line to <Stage>\policy-<RunId>.jsonl
# (hashes, PIDs, times, counts, categories, decisions; never a config value, key or log line).
#
# WHAT: host.mjs:148 builds the gate ONCE, at construction, from process.env (no runtime hot activation exists; agent.mjs has no
# route for it). Unset = OFF (book:null). The activation appends to node-config.local.cmd (updates never write it; node-config.cmd
# is regenerated by update-host.ps1) EXACTLY one of two pinned line sets:
#   option P   set ENCLAVE_PLATFORM_HOST_POLICY=production
#   option R   the same + set "ENCLAVE_PLATFORM_HOST_POLICY_RPCS=<the node's 5 repaired Base RPCs>"   (majority 3 of 5)
# and restarts ONLY the node agent (\Enclave\Node). The privacy agent, the manager, Hyper-V, every VM, privacy-config.json,
# run-node.cmd and node-config.cmd are never touched; their identities and hashes are post-checked.
# WHY THIS IS SAFE FOR THE WALLET HOLD: a stopped node retires nothing; its channel document lapses (<= 30 s) and the network then
# admits nothing (routes withdrawn, VMs kept by the manager); the new node writes a NEW generation EMPTY and re-grants on its first
# pass (the bounded app-traffic outage). The pinned nodeLog offset, the old generation and every expected id are journaled.
# THE GATE: an ON gate refuses service and renewals until its FIRST authenticated admit in the new process (no grace before it).
# So (1) BEFORE anything stops, the exact installed bundle proves admission with the exact appended environment (gate-proof.mjs,
# stdin, bounded child, nothing persisted); (2) the new node is accepted only when its lease pass is READY for every expected id
# (host.mjs leaseServing requires !platformPolicy.serviceRefusal(), so READY proves this process's gate admits) and the network
# applies its new channel generation.
# REVERT (one pass, the base's rules): node proven stopped -> node-config.local.cmd restored (CAS against the journaled after-sha,
# exact backup) -> node started -> its new generation applied. NEVER on an EXPLICIT platform refusal: when the new node's gate
# persisted a knownRefusal (ban, allowlist miss, deregistration, authority), turning the gate OFF would bypass the admin decision,
# so the policy line is KEPT, the node keeps running fail-closed and the run ends REFUSED_BY_POLICY (root/admin decide).
#  -Mode activate   pins -> prepared bytes in memory -> GATE PROOF -> BeforeStop -> stop -> backup + CAS append -> start ->
#                   READY + new generation applied -> observe re-grants -> post (DONE / DONE_PARTIAL / DONE_CHECK)
#  -Mode rollback   the explicit undo of a completed activation (refused while a platform refusal is persisted)
param([ValidateSet('activate','rollback')][string]$Mode = 'activate', [Parameter(Mandatory=$true)][string]$ParamsFile, [Parameter(Mandatory=$true)][string]$ParamsSha)
